WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.571
Welcome to Module 5: the Model Context Protocol, or MCP.

2
00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:10.460
It is an open standard for connecting AI applications to external tools and data.

3
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:24.030
You will learn what MCP is and why it is useful, how hosts, clients, and servers work together, and how to use the three server primitives, tools, resources, and prompts, in Python.

4
00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:32.210
You will follow one question through an interactive workflow, from the user to an external system and back.

5
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:38.610
Then you will read real JSON-RPC messages and build a server and client with the official Python SDK.

6
00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:48.510
The key takeaway: build a connector once as an MCP server, and any MCP-compatible application can use it, with your approval.
